Description: read-only system health checks for Linux
 Doctor NoX looks at the parts of a Linux system that tend to go wrong and
 explains what it finds: pending restarts, broken or half-installed packages,
 leftover config files, automatic updates, AppArmor or SELinux, the firewall,
 failed services, graphics drivers, game controllers, disk space, Flatpak and
 Snap, the network and boot errors.
 .
 It is strictly read-only: it never needs root, never changes the system and
 never makes network requests. It has a desktop window (needs PySide6) and a
 command line with text, JSON and redacted reports.
